# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# Item 738: the host declares `loc: merge A B`, a copy of two operands, writes
# `loc\value` and returns a nested method that reads it. The copy has no one
# named Structure for its type; its schema is the merge result's own. The
# reader of 40 gives 42. Entry 7.
A:
    int: value 0
end: A
B:
    int: other 5
end: B

fn: makeReader (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    loc: merge A B
    loc\value: n
    fn: read (int: x) int
        return: loc\value + x
    return: read

@: r40 makeReader(40)
int: a (r40: 2)
int: ok 7
if: a != 42
    ok: 1
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
